//==
// # The model mesh: types
//
// A model mesh is a finite 2-complex with a map to the exact model. Its 0-cells are the global
// vertices (Positions), its 2-cells the elements (Triangles, then Quads), and its 1-cells the
// undirected element sides, which MeshEdgeTable lists. Each vertex maps to a point of the model
// (VertexProvenance: a model vertex, a point of an edge's curve, a point of a face's surface), each
// element to the model face it approximates (ElementFace), and each element corner to the face's
// parameters and outward normal there (CornerUvs, CornerNormals).
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - The model mesh

//==
// # The model mesh

// The assembled mesh of a model (fixed by VOCABULARY.md). Indexing:
//  - per vertex (VertexIndex, numbered by Numbering): Positions, VertexProvenance;
//  - per element (ElementIndex: triangles first, then quads, so element T + q is quad q):
//    ElementFace, the model face the element approximates;
//  - per element corner (CornerIndex: corner 3t + s is slot s of triangle t, corner 3T + 4q + s is
//    slot s of quad q, T the triangle count): CornerNormals, the outward face normal of ElementFace
//    at the corner, and CornerUvs, the corner's parameters on ElementFace's surface. The uvs are
//    natural parameters (an angle in radians, a length), not the normalized ones the stdlib's
//    UvCoordinate comment describes.
// Corner attributes exist because one vertex can carry several values: two parameter values on a
// seam, one parameter pair per face on a model edge, one normal per face on a crease, one normal
// per element at a cone apex. Topology stays welded by index; only attributes are per corner.
// A quad is the two triangles of its A-C split wherever area, volume, or a conversion needs flat
// geometry, the split the stdlib's QuadFace comment and FanTriangles state.
type ModelMesh
    implements IValue
{
    Positions: Array<Point3D>;
    Triangles: Array<TriangleFace>;
    Quads: Array<QuadFace>;
    CornerNormals: Array<Direction3D>;
    CornerUvs: Array<UvCoordinate>;
    ElementFace: Array<BrepFaceIndex>;
    VertexProvenance: Array<MeshVertexProvenance>;
    Numbering: MeshVertexNumbering;
}
